<title>USA: Bill proposed to modify IRS payment system.</title>
<headline>Bill proposed to modify IRS payment system.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sen. Don Nickles, R-Oklahoma, said in a statement Friday he would introduce a bill to exempt most small businesses from an Internal Revenue Service order that they begin depositing their tax payments electronically by July 1.</p>
<p>Nickles' bill would phase in the electronic payment system requirement for large businesses and permanently exempt most small businesses.</p>
<p>&quot;Filing taxes electronically might very well be an option that many businesses would find helpful,&quot; Nickles said. &quot;But that should be a choice the individual makes based on what is best for his or her business.&quot;</p>
</text>
